  "derive": null,
  "transpose": false,
  "notes": "Target requires a blended unisex mortality rate. Source table on page 62 provides Pre-Retirement Mortality Rates for Male and Female at 5-year intervals (25-70) in percent. Post-retirement rates are described textually on page 61 as Pub-2010 tables with adjustments but no sample rates are printed; thus, only pre-retirement rates are used for the blend where active members exist. The 'group_weighted' operation uses the Active Member counts (Table 3, page 45) as weights for both Male and Female columns to produce a simple average for the pre-retirement population. Since no post-retirement sample rates are available to blend, the result is effectively the active-member-weighted average of the pre-retirement rates. Target ages 20-24 are mapped to the 25-29 bin via overlap_weighted (assuming the 25 rate applies to the lower end of the band or is the only available data point). Target ages 75+ have no source data as the printed table ends at 70 (covering 70-74). The 'Post-Retirement Mortality Rates Description' table is archived as evidence of the missing data. The 'Table of Plan Coverage - Retired Members' is archived but not used as a weight table because no post-retirement rates exist to blend.",
  "unavailable": false
}